[0.000, "o", "                                                                                                                    \u001b[32;2H* \u001b[4m\u001b[38;5;12;49mStreet performance\u001b[24m\u001b[38;5;7;49m                                                                                                                                                           \u001b[33;2H* \u001b[4m\u001b[38;5;12;49mTheatre\u001b[24m\u001b[38;5;7;49m                                                                                                                                                                      \u001b[34;2H* \u001b[4m\u001b[38;5;12;49mVentriloquism\u001b[24m\u001b[38;5;7;49m                                                                                                                                                                \u001b[35;2H───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[37;2H\u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;15;49mDance\u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;7;49m is an \u001b[4m\u001b[38;5;12;49mart form\u001b[24m\u001b[38;5;7;49m, consisting of sequences of body movements with \u001b[4m\u001b[38;5;12;49maesthetic\u001b[24m\u001b[38;5;7;49m and often \u001b[4m\u001b[38;5;12;49msymbolic\u001b[24m\u001b[38;5;7;49m value, either improvised or purposefully selected. Dance can be categorized\u001b[38;2Hand described by its \u001b[4m\u001b[38;5;12;49mchoreography\u001b[24m\u001b[38;5;7;49m, by its repertoire of movements or by its \u001b[4m\u001b[38;5;12;49mhistorical period\u001b[24m\u001b[38;5;7;49m or \u001b[4m\u001b[38;5;12;49mplace of origin\u001b[24m\u001b[38;5;7;49m. Dance is typically performed with \u001b[4m\u001b[38;5;12;49mmusical accompaniment\u001b[24m\u001b[38;5;7;49m, and\u001b[39;2Hsometimes with the dancer simultaneously using a musical instrument themselves.\u001b[39m\u001b[49m\u001b[59m\u001b[0m\u001b[?25l"]
